# Copy to .env and fill in real values. .env is gitignored - never commit it.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS FOR, AND WHAT IT IS NOT. Two things read .env:
#   - src/integrations/data.q, through .qdata.cfg, in any process.
#   - uqs (and uqs-mcp), which loads it, and .envrc through direnv, into every
#     process it starts. The environment uqs is started with wins over both
#     files, and .envrc wins over .env. See python/uqs/src/uqs/stack/envfiles.py.
# Anything started WITHOUT uqs - q run directly, scripts/test.py, the browser
# app - reads the OS environment only, so a key here that .qdata.cfg does not
# read is ignored there. That is why this template lists only those keys.
#
# The variables that DO NOT belong here, by theme:
#
#   Secrets - UQF_SOURCE_CRED_<SOURCE>, UQF_FRONTEND_GATEWAY_PASSWD.
#     Environment only, by rule: a file fallback is how a credential
#     ends up committed. `export` them in the shell that starts the process.
#     A gitignored .envrc (direnv) is the tidiest way to do that exporting:
#     your shell loads it on cd, and uqs loads it for every process it starts
#     even from a shell without direnv - always through direnv, so only after
#     `direnv allow`. Two reasons to prefer it over
#     typing the export. It UNLOADS when you leave the directory, so a stale
#     credential cannot outlive the shell that set it - re-pasting an older
#     `export` line and having it silently win is a real way to lose an
#     afternoon. And .envrc is executed, so a path can be derived rather
#     than pinned: CRYPTORUST_ROOT (see docs/reference/environment.md) is
#     enough to build the whole crypto_market_data credential.
#
#   Per-run arguments - UQF_DRY_RUN. It changes every invocation, so a
#     default in a file is a guess. The other per-run arguments are not
#     environment variables at all: a backfill's are `uqs backfill` flags,
#     the smoke check's are `scripts/test.py smoke` flags.
#
#   Deployment wiring - UQF_ROOT, UQF_STATUS_DIR, UQF_FRONTEND_*, UQF_API_ORIGIN.
#     The orchestrator's build_env() sets the first two for every TorQ
#     process; the service that starts the API sets the rest.
#
#   Developer knobs - Q, LOG_LEVEL, LOG_REGEX, CRYPTORUST_ROOT.
#     Shell-session settings. Export them, or put them in your shell profile.
#
# The full list, with who reads each: docs/reference/environment.md.
# scripts/gates/check_env_reference.py fails the commit if a key here is not read by .qdata.cfg.

# --- Local data paths ------------------------------------------------------

# Root folder containing Databento parquet dumps, one subfolder per symbol:
#   <DATABENTO_DATA_DIR>/<SYMBOL>/<SYMBOL>_<YYYY-MM-DD>_raw_mbp-10_us_hours.parquet
# Needed only when you load src/integrations/data.q, which src/init.q does
# not do. The OS environment takes precedence over this file.
DATABENTO_DATA_DIR=/path/to/databento/parquet/dumps
